        "original_id": "06d64baf-4d8c-5868-a32b-105e8db74d20",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: John Clare, Jonathan Bate, Matthew Allen\n- Organizations: University of Oxford, Worcester College Oxford, Warwick Business School\n- Places: High Beach\n- Works: The Quickening Maze\n- Roles: Professor of English Literature, Provost, Honorary Fellow of Creativity\n- Topics: mental asylum, English poetry, biography\n\nFacts:\n- In the late 1830s and 1840s, a mental asylum at High Beach was run by Matthew Allen.\n- In the late 1830s and 1840s, English poet John Clare was admitted to Matthew Allen's mental asylum at High Beach.\n- The Quickening Maze is based on the historical backdrop of Matthew Allen's mental asylum at High Beach in the late 1830s and 1840s.\n- Jonathan Bate is Professor of English Literature at the University of Oxford.\n- Jonathan Bate is Provost of Worcester College, Oxford.\n- Jonathan Bate is Honorary Fellow of Creativity at Warwick Business School.\n- Jonathan Bate is a biographer of John Clare.\n- Jonathan Bate stated that John Clare was \"the greatest labouring-class poet that England has ever produced.\"",
